<h2>Why we ride</h2>

<h3>Safe streets are a human right</h3>

<p>
  Everyone deserves to feel safe on the street, even and especially when they are not using a car.
</p>

<h3>People over machines</h3>

<p>
  We challenge car-centered design and planning, and we demand better from our leaders.
</p>

<h3>Accountable city leadership</h3>

<p>
  We want real traffic calming, protected bike lanes, actual bus rapid transit, and safe streets that protect people,
  not "traffic flow."
</p>

<h3>All on the same team</h3>

<p>
  This is not bike supremacy. Pedestrians, mobility-device users, bicycles, e-bikes, skaters, scooter riders, transit
  riders, and more all deserve safe, comfortable streets with dignity.
</p>

<h2>Want to lead a ride?</h2>

<p>
  Anyone can. Critical Mass has no governing body, and Denver Critical Mass isn't a chapter of anything. Plan and test
  the route first, then reach out at least one week ahead so we can coordinate details:
  <%= link_to "denvercriticalmass@gmail.com", "mailto:denvercriticalmass@gmail.com" %>.
</p>
